Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  

ORDER_ITEMS."status": filter to “Complete” line‑items  
ORDER_ITEMS."order_id": join key to ORDERS table  
ORDER_ITEMS."product_id": join key to PRODUCTS table, to aggregate sales volume  
ORDER_ITEMS."sale_price": sum to obtain revenue  
ORDER_ITEMS."created_at": time‑stamp (µs since epoch) – alternative to the ORDERS date  
ORDERS."order_id": primary key, keeps the whole order context  
ORDERS."status": filter to “Complete” orders (double check against ORDER_ITEMS)  
ORDERS."created_at": order time‑stamp (µs since epoch) – use to derive the sales month  
PRODUCTS."id": primary key (links to ORDER_ITEMS."product_id")  
PRODUCTS."name": product description for the report  
PRODUCTS."brand": must be not‑null; include in the final output  
PRODUCTS."category": include in the report  
PRODUCTS."department": optional extra grouping if needed  

------------------------------------------------------------------------
Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL snippets (each limited to 20 rows) that go from very simple inspections to a final, ready‑to‑run query that fulfils the business request.  
All identifiers are wrapped in double‑quotes.

```sql
-- 1️⃣ Description: Quick look at every distinct order status in ORDERS
SELECT DISTINCT "status"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDERS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2️⃣ Description: Distinct line‑item status codes in ORDER_ITEMS
SELECT DISTINCT "status"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3️⃣ Description: Sample of completed orders with their creation time (raw micro‑seconds)
SELECT "order_id",
       "created_at",
       "status"
FROM   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDERS"
WHERE  "status" = 'Complete'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4️⃣ Description: Peek at 20 completed line‑items and the product they reference
SELECT oi."order_id",
       oi."product_id",
       oi."sale_price",
       oi."created_at",
       p."name",
       p."brand",
       p."category"
FROM   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"  oi
JOIN   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"     p
       ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
WHERE  oi."status" = 'Complete'
  AND  p."brand" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
